        <p>PITTS'S announce Stocktaking to have been satisfactory beyond their fondest anticipations. Pitts's turnover during the past 12 months has increased by leaps and bounds and has exceeded that of any previous year by thousands of pounds. Pitts's strain every nerve to give each and every customer the utmost possible satisfaction ; and it is quite evident the public is fully alive to this fact. to judge from the startling increase in Pitts's business.Pitts's are constantly receiving congratulatory letters on their thorough and sys- tematic method of executing orders,which is. the writers say. in marked contrast to what is in vogue at rival establish- ments. Pitts's will ever use their best endeavours to supply good sound articles at moderate prices, as Pitts's axe confi4ent that this is the only royal road to success.</p>
        <p>IDITTS'S, ever on the alert, have secured, at merely nominal prices, some really magnificent Furniture, Pianos, Pictures, Bce., from the following iar..e mansions "Auburn House," "Woodlands," and ''Craigside," Southport; "Burlington House." Manchester; "Glen day," Didsbury; "Stamford House," Ashton; "nose Lea." Sale, au., lcc. To give an idea of the exceptionally high-class character of these goods, it may be stated that the sale at "Auburn House" alone realised several thousand pounds. Now Fitts's intend to promptly clear out these EXTRAORDINARY BAR- GAINS, giving their customers the benefit; so everyone desirous of beautifying their homes at a trifling cost with fur- nishings of a superlative excellence should visit Pitts's when they will certainly be delighted with the result. Pitta's will be very pleased indeed to show you round their vast estab- lishment, whether buying or not. Goods bought and not re- quired immediately can be warehoused any reasonable time and insured against fire free of charge. Cash prices only quoted, but deferred payment may be arranged.</p>
        <p>131 ITTS'S SAMPLE! BARQAINS, —Dining-room Suite, 1_ handsomest in Manchester, upholstered throughout with curled hair (guaranteed), small chairs, padded backs, magnificent sideboard fitted with bevelled glasses throughout, brackets. shelves, cupboards, cellarettes, ; extending table, with patent screw; overmautel, carnet, brass fender and brasses ; originally coat £l3O ; Pitts's price 62 guineas. Drawing-room Suite, Chippe, dale style, solid rosewood, beautifully inlaid with marqueterie work, upholstered throughont with curled hair (guaranteed), and covered in rich Genoa velvet; magnificent cabinet and overmantel, occasional, wine. and card tables, all inlaid to match ; carpet, rug, brass fender and brasses, clock and ornaments. com- plete ; cost £173; ritts's price 60 guineas. Bedroom Suite, solid throughout, consists of a very large wardrebe, with bevelled glass doors, drawers,cupbords, to. ; pair of large toilet tables, fitted with every convenience ; pedestal towel rail, and chairs Complete; a superb suite ; originally cost £B5 ; Pitts's price 35 guineas. Hundreds of other bargains on view, equally good value.</p>
        <p>PITTS'S HOUSH OP FUItbIiTURR, at 15f, 22f, 28f, 34, 50 up to 1,503 guineas are renowned far ad wide and are honestly worth double the price asked. Full particulars, press opinions and testimonials on application.</p>
        <p>pITTS'S CARPETS —Largest and best selected Stock of Brussels, Tapestry, Axmlnster. Wilton, Velvet Pile. &amp;c.. Linoleum. Flooreloths, o, ll English manufacture, at exceptionally low prices to clear. Fitted free of charge.</p>
        <p>PITTS'S PlANOS.—Thnroughly Reliable. new and second- hand by Collard and Collard, Kirkman,Brard, Wernam. Dalmaine and other good makers, splendid selection, Utmost Value. Guargateel Great Savkg.</p>
