      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1898-01-28_WidnesExaminer_art0067" n="art0067">
        <head>BEAR THIS IN MIND.</head>
        <p>BEAR THIS IN MIND.</p>
        <p>A " Cold " is not necessarily the result cf a high or low temperature. A person may go directly from a hot bath directly into a cold one, or into snow even,and not take cold. Be may remain out in the coldest atmos- phere until chilled through, and still not take cold. On the contary, he may take cold by pouring a couple of teaspoonfuls of water upon some part of his dress, or by standing in a door or before the stove, or by sitting near a window or other opening. where roe part of the body is colder than the ot, er part. Let it ha kept in mind that unifArmity of t..,^nerature over the whole body is the great thing to be 1 ked after. It is the unequal heat upon different part, =f the body that produces Colds by disturbing uni . n circulation of the blood, which in turn induces con-Lion of some part. Keep the feet always dry and warm, avoid draughts of air, keep the system braced up by plenty of sleep and good food and by a powerful Tonic, and you will be proof against a Cold and its results. The very beat Medicine either for preventing or curing a Cold, is GWILYM EVANS' QUININE BITTERS, o THE VEGATABLE TONIC,</p>
        <p>Which is the most perfect Vegetable Remedy known,and the most efficacious to strengthen the constitution, en- liven the drooping or depressed spirits,brace the erves, and remove all Disorders of the Stomach which are caused by Indigestion, such as Loss of Appetite, distre,s after Eating, Acidity of Stomach,Eructation, Heaviness and Langour. Disorders of the Liver are often caused by defective Digestion. The potency of the gastric juice in the process of Digestion is wonderfully aided by the powertil ingredients contained in GWILYM EVANS' QUININE BIT MRS. While the Stomach recovers its normal tone, the putrid ndigested food is cleared away, and the poor dysp-p- -tic is relieved of his load of misery, once more and en- joys go d health and looks forward to happiness and lonry, life. If tour occupation is an unhealthy one, if you are ex- posed to the weather, or work long hours in close rooms if your constitution is weakened, er your health under- mined ; or if yeu are in any NV4V not" up to the mark," use G wilym Evans' Quinine Bitters. It never fails to strengthen the weakened system, to brace the nerves, ' and fortify the constitution. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is purely veget -dale and certified by Analysts to be pure and harmless. It may be safely taken by delicate ladies and children in all cases of weakness. It is sold in Betties, at 2s. 9d. and 4s. W. each, by all Chemists and Patent Medicine Vendors, or direct from the Proprietors,The Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Corn pany Ltd.. Lianelly, South Wales, Carriage Free b Parcels Post. P 'ware of Inait,td-ins. See the nana " Gwilyrn Eva i "on Label, Stamp, Bottle.</p>
