        <p>HOW TO GRT A BILLIARD TABLU FOR 18s. 6d. GEORGE G. BUSSEY AND Co., of 36 and 38. Queen Victeria-street, Louden, make an ingenious set of arrange- ments whereby a good game of Billiards can be played on an ordinary dining table. The fittings are easily fixed, and do no damage to the table. The price includes everything required to play the game. Ask the local Sports Dealer for descriptiv e pamplet. (2). Secretaries of Football Chiba are requested to note the reports of matches played on Saturday must be sent to Eh Head Office. Bowsey-street, Warrington not later than 1 o'clockoia Thursday morning or they cannot beser inted .</p>
