        <p>--- The announcement that Mr. Wallace Reville, proprie-• tor of the S. Helens Theatre Royal, has arranged for a return visit of "Tie Sign of The Cross " has given general satisfaction to his patrons in the town. On the, last occasion the theatre was crowded at each perfor• mance, and many persons were disappointed in being unable to gain admission. The company is an exception- ally strong one, under the management of Mr. William Greet, and the remarkable play will be produced with all its beautiful scenery and other acccs4ories. Partied- bars appear in an advertisemrnt in Another column.</p>
