        <p>PADOATE. SUNDAY SCHOOL TEA. PARTY.—The Sunday School tea-- party in connection with Christ Cnurch took place on. Friday last week. The scholars partook of tea in the schoolroom in the afternoon, after which all kinds 0 games were indulged in until seven o'clock when an en tertainment was given. Songs, gleQs,dialogues,etc,were rendered by the Sunday school scholars, the pror4ramme also including items by Misses Turner, Barnes, Florridge, Messrs B. Harding and R. Smith. An amusing dialogue "The Irish Schoolmaster" was gone through by Mr. E; C. Lovering and scholars and a cantata" Queen of the Flowers " by a number of little girls. The prizes for regular attendance were distributed by Miss Saunders. The concert closed with the singing of the National Anthem after which nuts, oranges.etc,were given to the members of the Sunday school.</p>
